,"global_rank":125043},{"name":"fabricekalvanda/quilts","owner":"fabricekalvanda","html_url":"https://github.com/fabricekalvanda/quilts","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"I have a business that sells quilts of the same pattern, but different sizes depending on the customers needs. A customer is able to request a quilt with this pattern as big as they want.","topics":[],"score":226804,"global_rank":125044},{"name":"fabricekalvanda/diceGame","owner":"fabricekalvanda","html_url":"https://github.com/fabricekalvanda/diceGame","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"I have 2 die, 6 sided each I start the game and print the intro  \u201cHey! Welcome to Tina\u2019s Dice Game.\u201d \u201cLet\u2019s start!\u201d The computer randomly generates what side of the die is chosen (for each die) I then add both of the random numbers together  I then print  Dice 1 = (the random number I got)  Dice 2 = (the random number I got) Depending on what number I get, something different is printed to the screen If I get an even number  I print \u201cI got (value of dice 1) and (value of dice 2)!\u201d  I print \u201cEvens are better than odds!\u201d If I get an odd number I print \u201cI got (value of dice 1) and (value of dice 2)!\u201d  I print \u201cOdds are still cool!\u201d At the end, I ask the user if they want to play again If the answer is \u201cYES\u201d  I \u201cthrow\u201d the die again and repeat the printing process If the answer is anything but YES (case-sensitive) I end the game and print the outro  \u201cThe number of times the dice was thrown is: (value of times dice is thrown)\u201d \u201cNice game!\u201d \u201cThanks for playing, Come play again soon!\u201d\u2028","topics":[],"score":226804,"global_rank":125045},{"name":"xeniaeo/stay-apart-game","owner":"xeniaeo","html_url":"https://github.com/xeniaeo/stay-apart-game","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"A Ludum Dare 46 submission","topics":[],"score":226800,"global_rank":125074},{"name":"GregBahm/PokerVis","owner":"GregBahm","html_url":"https://github.com/GregBahm/PokerVis","stars":0,"forks":1,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"Visualize the win probabilities of poker hands","topics":[],"score":226800,"global_rank":125078},{"name":"mluanastevensc/CSharp_FactoryPattern","owner":"mluanastevensc","html_url":"https://github.com/mluanastevensc/CSharp_FactoryPattern","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":null,"topics":[],"score":226800,"global_rank":125090},{"name":"arthur-ryoo/CarDealership-API","owner":"arthur-ryoo","html_url":"https://github.com/arthur-ryoo/CarDealership-API","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":null,"topics":[],"score":226800,"global_rank":125096},{"name":"ronbrogan/Azure-StorageEmulator-StaticSite","owner":"ronbrogan","html_url":"https://github.com/ronbrogan/Azure-StorageEmulator-StaticSite","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"A tool to create and serve content from your local Azure Storage Emulator instance for development purposes","topics":[],"score":226791,"global_rank":125138},{"name":"leggomyfroggo/FroggoTetrisAttack","owner":"leggomyfroggo","html_url":"https://github.com/leggomyfroggo/FroggoTetrisAttack","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"Tetris Attack or Puzzle League game created in MonoGame.","topics":["hacktoberfest"],"score":226791,"global_rank":125161},{"name":"arthur-ryoo/.NetCoreQuestionsApp","owner":"arthur-ryoo","html_url":"https://github.com/arthur-ryoo/.NetCoreQuestionsApp","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"A web database app in ASP.NET Core.","topics":[],"score":226790,"global_rank":125243},{"name":"mikehall-ms/FlipdotEmulator","owner":"mikehall-ms","html_url":"https://github.com/mikehall-ms/FlipdotEmulator","stars":0,"forks"